{
  "id": "polar_vs__cartesian_coordinates",
  "title": "Polar vs. Cartesian Coordinates",
  "description": "Convert between Polar and Cartesian coordinate systems. Transform 2D coordinates using mathematical formulas to switch between perpendicular Cartesian axes and distance/angle-based Polar coordinates.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Polar vs. Cartesian Coordinates\n\nIn the Cartesian system the coordinates are perpendicular to one another with the same unit length on both axes.\n\n**2D Cartesian coordinates**: (x, y)\n\nA Polar coordinate system is determined by a fixed point (origin or pole) and a zero direction (axis). Each point is determined by an angle and a distance relative to the zero axis and the origin.\n\n**Polar coordinates**: (r, θ)\n\n### Conversion Formulas\n\n**Cartesian to Polar:**\n- r = √(x² + y²)\n- θ = atan(y / x)\n\n**Polar to Cartesian:**\n- x = r cos(θ)\n- y = r sin(θ)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Cartesian to Polar Coordinates"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "cartesian_x",
          "label": "X Coordinate",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "cartesian_y",
          "label": "Y Coordinate",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 3
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "polar_r",
          "label": "Distance (r)",
          "unit": "units",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.cartesian_x ** 2 + inputs.cartesian_y ** 2)"
        },
        {
          "id": "polar_theta",
          "label": "Angle (θ)",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "Math.atan(inputs.cartesian_y / inputs.cartesian_x) * (180 / Math.PI)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Polar to Cartesian Coordinates"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "polar_r_input",
          "label": "Distance (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 3.6,
          "unit": "units"
        },
        {
          "id": "polar_theta_input",
          "label": "Angle (θ)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 56.31,
          "unit": "degrees"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "cartesian_x_result",
          "label": "X Coordinate",
          "unit": "units",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.polar_r_input * Math.cos(inputs.polar_theta_input * (Math.PI / 180))"
        },
        {
          "id": "cartesian_y_result",
          "label": "Y Coordinate",
          "unit": "units",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.polar_r_input * Math.sin(inputs.polar_theta_input * (Math.PI / 180))"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}